[planner -> lidar] PLAN REVIEW REQUEST — do NOT execute yet. Check only YOUR specialty (navigator / lidar / camera). Prefer ZERO tools; reply AGREE: or DISAGREE: in one line.

SPECIALIST PLAN:
Plan to visit in order: 1) nearest rock, 2) nearest container, 3) nearest car.

High-level loop (repeat per target until confirmed):
- At each stopped pose, lidar and camera will sense (lidar: get_semantic_lidar_objects; camera: capture image/histogram).
- If lidar returns a centroid for the current target class, the planner will compute a navigation goal at least 3.0 m from that centroid, offset toward spawn (0,0): goal = centroid + 3.0*(spawn - centroid)/||spawn - centroid||. Navigator will navigate_to_pose that goal. After the navigator reports success, lidar (preferred) will call confirm_stop(<class>) to verify the stop. If confirm_stop returns true, mark target visited and proceed to next target. If navigation fails, request occupancy map and replan a different viewpoint.
- If lidar does not report the target centroid, navigator will move to the next exploration viewpoint (sequence of waypoints: (3,0), (0,3), (-3,0), (0,-3), then repeat) and we will sense again. Use get_occupancy_map only after a nav failure or if we need an alternate free-cell viewpoint.

Roles:
- navigator: execute navigate_to_pose goals provided by planner. Do not attempt sensing or confirming. Reach within ~2.5 m is sufficient for success.
- lidar: when asked at a stop, run get_semantic_lidar_objects and return any centroids. After a navigator success at a planned goal, run confirm_stop(<class>) to verify the ordered stop (or confirm upon request if camera cannot). Lidar is the preferred confirmer.
- camera: at each stop capture an image and optionally return a class histogram. If lidar cannot confirm a stop, camera may call confirm_stop(<class>) as a fallback.

Constraints: never navigate to an object centroid; all nav goals will be >=3.0 m from any reported centroid. Use occupancy map only when exploring or after nav failures. Continue until all three ordered classes (rock, container, car) are confirmed. After every ordered stop is confirmed, planner will call report_mission_done with a short summary of visited classes in order.

